10308 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Instead of opening the front door\054 they sit at their desk and open their laptop\056 Instead of pressing elevator buttons\054 they click the login button\073 instead of passing through security gates\054 they navigate login screens\056 This is a commute for survival\024one in which humanity has begun commuting into games\056\n\nWe stand at the intersection of two massive curves\056 On one side\054 the Great Replacement is underway\056 Automation and artificial intelligence \050AI\051 are rapidly erasing human jobs through warehouse robots\054 autonomous vehicles\054 and generative AI\056 On the other side\054 the Great Migration begins\056 Games\054 platforms\054 and the metaverse are no longer mere spaces for leisure\073 they are becoming the foundation of virtual economies where income\054 assets\054 and sometimes even survival itself are at stake\056\n\nThese shifts have manifested repeatedly throughout history\056 When economies falter\054 people lose their livelihoods and relocate in search of new opportunities for survival\056 Just as farmers displaced by industrialization were pushed into factory districts and transformed into urban laborers\054 labor has always been redistributed toward where capital and opportunity flow\056 The \034item farms1\051\035 that shook Korea\031s online gaming market\054 and the surge of labor in virtual worlds during the COVID\05519 pandemic\054 emerged from this same trajectory\056 These were decisive signals of where human movement turns when physical workplaces shrink\024and how labor is reinvented within the uncharted territory of the virtual world\056\n\nThis article aims to peel back the veneer of terms such as \034P2E \050Play\055to\055Earn\051\035 and \034X2E2\051\035\054 which have become marketing buzzwords\054 and to confront them instead as a social phenomenon of digital labor\056 Its goal is to dissect these early signals of future labor and to articulate what is required for those displaced from the physical economy during the AI transition to establish sustainable foundations within virtual economies\056\n\nTo this end\054 we first examine the moment digital labor emerges through the cases of the online games Lineage in Korea and RuneScape in Venezuela\056 We then analyze the structural contradictions of mining\055type games and the \034nomad versus settler\035 dynamic through the rise and fall of Axie Infinity\056 Next\054 by broadening our perspective\054 we explore how populations displaced during the AI transition may diversify into various forms of digital labor\056 Finally\054 drawing on the economic model of Roblox and the meme token BONK within the Solana ecosystem\054 we investigate the conditions for X2E 2\0560\024a model capable of transforming nomads into settlers\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 10309 0 R
     /Pg 1390 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

