10323 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In 1998\054 South Korea was engulfed by the shockwaves of the IMF foreign exchange crisis\056 Companies collapsed\054 and countless breadwinners were pushed out of the labor market\056 At the time\054 Korea\031s minimum wage hovered at little more than one dollar per hour\056I Against this backdrop\054 an online game emerged with a seemingly absurd price tag of twenty dollars per monthII\072 NCSoft\031s Lineage\056\n\nGiven the high cost of internet access and the desperation of the economic climate\054 the game\031s success appeared highly unlikely\056 Yet Lineage became both an escape from reality and a new field of opportunity for the unemployed and for young men drifting between PC bangs\024Korean internet gaming caf\351s\056 This virtual land attracted both those rich in time and those wielding purchasing power\056 Before long\054 an economic system that closely mirrored the real world began to take shape\056\n\nThe core structure of Lineage can be described as a form of digital feudalism\056 When a Blood Alliance captures a castle through siege warfare\054 the ruling lord gains the authority to set tax rates within that territory\056 A portion of the currency spent by players buying and selling consumables\024such as potions\024in castle shops is collected as tax revenue\056 Siege warfare\054 therefore\054 is not merely a contest of honor\054 but a fierce struggle for control over the flow of in\055game currency \050Adena\051 circulating within the territory\056\n\nThe ruler who claims a castle effectively becomes the head of a local government\054 using vast tax revenues to recruit clan members and expand political and military power\056 Ordinary players\054 in turn\054 become taxpayers who sustain this system through everyday consumption\056 Lineage thus reproduces one of the harshest formulas of real\055world politics and capitalism\072 power grants the right to allocate resources\056\n\nIn this fierce power struggle\054 the value of in\055game items symbolizing strength skyrocketed\056 From early high\055enhancement weapons to the Executioner Sword\054 which later emerged as the pinnacle of Lineage\031s economy\054 rare items were far more than mere pixels\056 Crafting the Executioner Sword required tens of thousands of repeated hunts over several months\056 Moreover\054 the success rate of enhancement plummeted with each higher level\054 while the risk of item destruction )
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 10324 0 R
     /Pg 1652 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

