10332 0 obj
  << /ActualText (destruction upon failure further inflated the value of highly enhanced swords to extreme levels\056III Supply was tightly constrained\054 while demand from those craving absolute power exploded\056 As a result\054 the saying \034A highly enhanced Executioner Sword costs as much as a house\035 became an accepted fact\056 The Executioner Sword even earned the nickname \034house\055selling sword\054\035 meaning a weapon so expensive that one might have to sell a house to acquire it\056 This served as a signal flare\054 announcing that labor and time invested in the virtual world had begun to convert into real\055world monetary value\056\n\nThe fundamental question\024\034Why are game items so expensive\077\035\024became a luxury\056 In its place emerged a more urgent concern\072 \034How much of my real\055world debt could I pay off if I sold this sword right now\077\035 This peculiar economy\054 born from the unique conditions of the IMF economic crisis\054 was an unprecedented real\055time social experiment\056\n\nLineage lays bare how power and capital operate through scarce resources when capital\055rich players and time\055rich workers meet within a virtual nation\056 The prototype of what we now call Play\055to\055Earn \050P2E\051 is already present here\056 Decades before grand technological terms such as blockchain or token economies entered popular discourse\054 Korean gamers were already commuting to work through games\056 The era of subsistence gaming had dawned\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10333 0 R
     /Pg 2112 0 R
