10378 0 obj
  << /ActualText (recently\054 digital files could be replicated endlessly\054 rendering the very notion of an \034original\035 ambiguous\056 Blockchain technology resolves this problem by assigning a unique identifier to each asset\054 transforming it into a singular\054 verifiable digital object\056 In effect\054 the digital world has acquired its own system of official registration\056\n\nThis shift is revolutionary\056 It marks a transfer of ownership from platforms to individuals\056 Whereas Web 2\0560 assets were confined within corporate servers\054 Web 3\0560 NFT assets exist in the public domain of the blockchain\056 Even if a game company goes bankrupt and its services shut down\054 the ownership record of an NFT stored in a personal wallet persists\054 so long as the blockchain network itself continues to operate\056 Admittedly\054 if the game associated with an item disappears\054 its functional or utility value may collapse\056 Yet this represents a fundamentally different condition\072 while usefulness may vanish\054 proof of ownership does not\056\n\nIt is only upon this technological foundation that the concept of Play\055to\055Earn \050P2E\051 truly takes shape\056 If cash transactions during the Lineage era resembled a form of \034smuggling\035 prohibited by game companies\054 blockchain\055based P2E has transformed this activity into legitimate trade\056 Players mine tokens or NFTs through gameplay\054 transfer them to their personal wallets\054 and cash them out instantly\024without requiring permission\024via decentralized exchanges \050DEXs\051 or marketplaces such as OpenSea\056 Under these conditions\054 company policies such as \034cash transactions are prohibited\035 become largely meaningless\056 Asset transfers occur directly between users through peer\055to\055peer \050P2P\051 networks\054 without passing through any central server\056 In this way\054 P2E elevates player activity from an illicit workaround to a recognized form of digital economic participation\056\n\nHowever\054 while blockchain resolves the problem of ownership\054 it does not resolve the problem of value\056 Although the fact that an NFT belongs to its holder is immutable\054 whether that NFT is worth one thousand dollars or mere ten cents depends entirely on market supply and demand\054 as well as the underlying economic design of the game\056\nIn a gold mine where everyone extracts resources but no one consumes them\054 gold ultimately becomes worthless\024regardless of who owns it\056 Technology only creates the vessel\073 what fills it belongs to the domain of economics and governance\056 The speed with which technology can devolve into disaster when this fundamental truth is ignored will soon be illustrated by a vast experimental laboratory known as Axie Infinity\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10379 0 R
     /Pg 2790 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
