10441 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The greatest mistake made by early P2E projects\054 including Axie Infinity\054 was treating everyone on the screen as a single category\072 \034gamers\056\035 Project teams proudly claimed that \034millions log in every day\054\035 but that mass of users was never a uniform group\056 In reality\054 it was divided into two fundamentally different types of participants\054 distinguished by motivation\072 nomads and settlers\056\n\nThe first group\054 nomads\054 are both investors and miners\056 To them\054 the game is not a playground but a factory\024a temporary site for extracting profit\056 They have little interest in the game\031s world\054 lore\054 or characters\056 Their only concern is return on investment\072 How many hours must I work to recover my initial capital\054 and how much can I earn after that\077 Nomads are cold\054 rational economic actors\056 They inject capital and activity into the ecosystem to generate short\055term liquidity\054 then leave without hesitation the moment returns begin to decline\056\n\nSettlers\054 by contrast\054 stay up late playing with friends and willingly open their wallets to customize their characters\056 For them\054 tokens are not wages to be immediately sold but tickets to a richer experience\056 From an economic standpoint\054 settlers resemble tourists who spend money earned outside the game inside the game world\056 They also serve as a buffer that mitigates inflationary pressure on the in\055game currency\056 Without settlers\054 the products of nomads\031 labor cannot retain value\056\240\n\nA healthy in\055game economy emerges only when these two groups coexist in proper balance\056 Axie Infinity\031s population structure\054 however\054 had completely lost that balance\056 It was as if 990\054000 people in a city of one million were all trying to sell\054 with almost no one left to buy\056 The moment new inflows slowed\054 a digital bank run began\024a borderless exodus\056 Unlike real nations\054 digital nations have no gravity\056 In the physical world\054 even when an economy collapses\054 people cannot abandon their country overnight\056 Borders\054 visas\054 and the ties of family and community hold them in place\056 In a digital nation\054 none of these frictions exist\056 The instant profitability drops and the reason to log in disappears\054 it takes less than a minute to delete the app and move on to the next game down the hall offering higher returns\056 When token prices collapsed and the cost\055effectiveness of labor fell below that of alternative jobs\054 the vast Axie empire emptied out in a matter of weeks\056 The servers continued to run and the blockchain records remained intact\054 but the economy\024and the society that once breathed within it\024had already evaporated\056\n)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 10442 0 R
     /Pg 3852 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

10442 0 obj
