10469 0 obj
  << /ActualText (If Axie Infinity serves as a cautionary tale of a digital nation\031s rapid collapse\054 the intersection of the British MMORPG RuneScape and the Venezuelan economic crisis reveals a very different trajectory\056 n the late 2010s\054 Venezuela was engulfed in a period of brutal hyperinflation\056 Prices rose by millions of percent\054 and it was common for price tags to change while people were standing in line at supermarket checkouts\056 Instead of counting banknotes\054 people weighed them on scales\054 and burning bundles of cash became more common than buying firewood\056\n\nTo survive\054 young Venezuelans chose a form of digital exile\056 Their destination was RuneScape\054 a classic MMORPG released in 2001 by the British developer Jagex\054 known for its crude graphics\056 In shabby internet caf\351s and homes across Caracas\054 countless youths hunted monsters to accumulate in\055game \034gold\056\035X Their goal was not leveling up or climbing rankings\056 They sold the gold they mined through black\055market channels in exchange for dollars or Bitcoin\054 which they used to buy real\055world groceries\056XI For these \034gold farmers\054\035 RuneScape became the only factory that paid wages\056\n\nWhat matters here is not a romantic claim that \034game money replaced fiat currency\056\035 Rather\054 in a moment of national crisis\054 RuneScape gold functioned as an alternative income source and a minimal store of value for young Venezuelans\056 Compared to the speed at which the bol\355var disintegrated into worthless paper\054 the game\031s internal exchange order and gold prices remained relatively predictable\056 Of course\054 game money was not without risk\072 prices fluctuated\054 and account bans or scams were constant threats\056 Still\054 players entered the game servers in search of something less volatile than their collapsing national currency\056 Ironically\054 the economic order of a single online game partially filled the void left by the state\031s failure to provide monetary stability\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 10470 0 R
     /Pg 4574 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

