10488 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Although both Axie Infinity and RuneScape experienced massive influxes of subsistence\055type users\054 their fates diverged dramatically\056 Axie\031s economy collapsed within a year\054 while RuneScape remains resilient to this day\056 How was the RuneScape market able to withstand the gold\055supply shock unleashed by Venezuelan players\077\n\nThe answer lies in its foundational design\056 The secret to RuneScape\031s longevity is that it was never built as a money\055making venture in the first place\056 Having operated continuously since 2001\054 the game had already cultivated a deep\055rooted community of \034settlers\035 long before Venezuelans entered the scene\056 These settlers included working professionals in North America and Europe\054 as well as older gamers returning out of nostalgia\056 For them\054 RuneScape was not a workplace\054 but a place to unwind after work\054 perhaps with a beer\056 These Western settlers had disposable income but little time\056 They wanted to skip tedious gathering and grinding\054 and they were willing to open their wallets to do so\056 This is precisely where Venezuelan gold farmers\024rich in time but poor in capital\024entered the picture\056 What emerged was a near\055perfect international division of labor\056 Even as the number of Venezuelan workers surged\054 the strong and persistent demand for gold absorbed the supply shock and kept the economy in motion\056\n\nUltimately\054 it was economic flow that determined the outcome\056 RuneScape\031s economy formed a healthy circular structure\072\nSettlers\031 demand \222 Venezuelan mining \222 Settlers\031 consumption\056\nBy contrast\054 Axie Infinity followed a linear and fragile path\072\nNomads\031 mining \222 Selling \222 Price collapse \222 Nomads\031 exit\056\nBecause speculation and cashing out\024not consumption\024sat at the center of Axie\031s economy\054 the system lost its reason to exist the moment prices fell\056\n\nThe success of any X2E model does not hinge on how many people join\056 It depends on how many settlers exist who are willing to buy and use what nomads produce\056 What sustains a virtual world is not labor performed out of necessity\054 but enjoyment and meaning that people are willing to pay for in order to stay\056 A world without this foundation is nothing more than a sandcastle\054 inevitably washed away by the tide\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 10489 0 R
     /Pg 4886 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

