10501 0 obj
  << /ActualText (For a resident of Caracas\054 it can be a full day\031s food budget for an entire family\056 This massive arbitrage of monetary value is unfolding in real time\054 mediated by games\056\n\nThis class\055based division of labor was never an explicit design goal\056 Lineage\031s \034workshops\054\035 RuneScape\031s gold farmers\054 and Axie Infinity\031s scholarship system were all spontaneous orders produced by the invisible hand of the market\056 They emerged as real\055world inequality seeped across digital borders\056\n\nWhat matters is that this landscape is not merely a historical curiosity\056 It is a structural preview of the coming AI era\056 As artificial intelligence and robotic automation erase physical jobs\054 digital migration will become unavoidable for those displaced from the real economy\056 The moment when the internet reorganizes itself into a single\054 transnational labor market is approaching rapidly\056 The class structure of this market is already visible\056 Citizens of advanced economies\054 able to trade capital for time\054 will remain consumers\056 Those who connect out of necessity will become a digital proletariat\054 mining resources\054 training models\054 and performing data labeling in virtual mines\056 We must neither passively despair at this trend nor romanticize it as a \034utopia where everyone earns money\056\035 The real question is how to govern this inequality\056 What rules are needed to prevent real\055world disparities from hardening into exploitation in virtual space\024and instead turn virtual economies into genuine ladders of social mobility\077 This is the philosophical question that must come first when designing X2E systems and the virtual economies that follow\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10502 0 R
     /Pg 5214 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

