10537 0 obj
  << /ActualText (slum or the Kenyan countryside\024one can enter new economic territories with a single click\056 This near\055zero barrier to entry creates a paradoxical landscape\056 Those expelled first from the real labor market\024people in developing nations lacking capital\054 formal credentials\054 or passport power\024become the vanguard of digital labor\056 Those with nowhere left to go in the physical world are the first to plant their flags in virtual space\056\n\nBut they do not settle\056 Instead\054 they become algorithmic nomads\054 perpetually on the move\056 When Axie Infinity\031s returns fall\054 they migrate to another game like MIR4\056 When in\055game item prices collapse\054 they pack up and shift to TikTok challenges\054 click\055work platforms\054 or data\055labeling apps\056 They remain only as long as the platform\031s tokenomics or algorithms make survival rational\056\n\nThe crucial point is that this is not merely a tragic story unfolding in developing countries\056 These populations have simply reached the edge of the chasm a little earlier than the rest of us\056 As AI begins to replace not only factory labor but office and professional work\054 the middle class in advanced economies will confront the same reality\056 In a future where factory gates and office doors are closed\054 leaving only server ports open\054 humanity will wake each morning to a new calculation\072 Which platform do I commute to today\077 And\054 more urgently still\072 Within that platform\054 what can I sell to survive\077)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10538 0 R
     /Pg 5904 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

