10545 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Just because everyone migrates into the same digital world does not mean they survive in the same way\056 Even if they turn on the same screen\054 connect to the same server\054 and play the same game\054 the reward structures and competitive pressures they face are fundamentally different\056 Digital labor will not converge into a single occupation\056 Instead\054 it will evolve into a complex ecosystem where multiple economic logics coexist\056 An individual\031s survival will depend on how quickly they can read the rules of the system\054 how flexibly they adapt\054 and how long they can endure within it\056\n\nIn the AI era\054 digital labor is likely to crystallize into four distinct types\072 extractive labor\054 market\055making\054 audience\055building\054 and generative creation\056\n\nExtractive labor refers to primitive\054 repetitive work such as resource gathering and grinding\024exemplified by SLP mining in Axie Infinity or gold farming in RuneScape\056 What is required here is not skill or creativity\054 but endurance\072 the ability to tolerate repetition and sustained clicking\056 This form of labor is easily replaceable\056 It is vulnerable to wage compression toward low\055cost regions and\054 ultimately\054 to AI and bot automation\056 While human hands are still required due to bot\055detection systems and enforcement by game companies\054 the moment automation costs fall further and evasion techniques improve\054 workers in this category are likely to lose their footing\056\n\nThe second type is market\055making\056 As automation accelerates and traditional jobs disappear\054 the population living inside games will expand\054 and with it\054 markets for in\055game assets\056 Labor here does not involve producing goods directly\054 but managing value\024reading market signals\054 evaluating scarcity\054 and reallocating assets\056 However\054 this domain carries profound ownership risks\056 The recent case of Counter\055Strike7\051 illustrates the problem\056 In October 2025\054 Valve )
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 10546 0 R
     /Pg 5904 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

